# Canonicalize on the non-trailing-slash form everywhere. Every canonical
# tag and internal link on the site uses the non-slash form, but Cloudflare
# Pages' default asset routing serves directory-style pages (slug/index.html)
# at the trailing-slash URL and only 307s the non-slash request onward —
# the opposite direction. That left every blog post's canonical tag pointing
# at a URL that immediately redirected away from itself, splitting ranking
# signal across two URLs for the same page. This rule takes precedence over
# that default (redirects are always followed ahead of asset matching) and
# forces the single direction the rest of the site already assumes.
/*/ /:splat 301
